---
source: crates/specforge-cli/src/main.rs
expression: command.clone().render_long_help().to_string()
---
Render the logical data model (entity kinds, fields, relationships)

Usage: specforge model [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --path <PATH>
          A path inside the project (the nearest directory at or above it holding specforge.json; none: the directory itself, with the default configuration)
          
          [default: .]

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - markdown
          - mermaid:  ER diagram
          - dot:      Graphviz
          - json
          - dbml:     dbdiagram.io
          
          [default: markdown]

      --group-by <GROUP_BY>
          How to group entities

          Possible values:
          - extension: under a header per extension
          - none:      one flat list
          
          [default: extension]

      --fields <FIELDS>
          Field detail level

          Possible values:
          - none
          - keys: key fields
          - all
          
          [default: keys]

      --extension <EXTENSION>
          Filter to a single extension

      --kinds <KINDS>
          Filter to specific entity kinds (comma-separated)

      --root <ROOT>
          Root entity kind for depth-scoped output

      --depth <DEPTH>
          Maximum depth from root kind (requires --root)

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
